            title: 'High Fives Dominoes',
            subtitle: 'Card game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'High Fives Dominoes is a western domino connecting game played with a double-15 set, using the extended value range to create longer sessions and more complex end control. Players match open ends while managing mobility and high-value risk, since high numbers can amplify blocking and pip exposure outcomes.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'High Fives Dominoes is encountered as a modern extended-set format that relies on large western domino sets for long sessions and larger groups.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '2 to 10 players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'One double-15 western domino set.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Domino set and optional score tracking by match profile.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Deal tiles by player count; remaining tiles form a boneyard if the profile uses draws.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
